---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → native; verified by the executed swift test below)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  shell:  isLoading ? <DriveDetailSkeleton> : <PageContainer title error actions>
            → DriveDetailPageModel.Phase switch: .loading → DriveDetailPageSkeleton
              (TSPageHeaderSkeleton + TSStatGridSkeleton + 2× TSChartBlockSkeleton);
              .error → DriveDetailPageErrorView (danger glyph + message + Retry →
              model.refresh()); .empty → DriveDetailPageEmptyView
              (ContentUnavailableView); .content → the composed section stack.
  envelope: hasTelemetryRows = telemetry.length>0 || positions.length>0;
            hasMeaningfulDriveStats = (distanceM ?? 0)>0 || (stats.maxSpd ?? 0)>0
              || (stats.energyWh ?? 0)>0 || hasTelemetryRows
            → DriveDetailProjector.project(_:) reproduces this VERBATIM (pinned by
              DriveDetailProjectorTests, 9/9). vehicleName = display_name ||
              t('driveDetail.vehicle','Vehicle').
  banner: !hasMeaningfulDriveStats → <AlertBanner variant="info"
            title=noTelemetryTitle>{noTelemetryBody}</AlertBanner>
            → DriveDetailNoTelemetryBanner (info-tinted card, info.circle.fill,
              title + body) gated by DriveDetailSectionPlan.showsNoTelemetryBanner.
  sections: each web <SectionErrorBoundary name=… fallbackTitle=t('driveDetail.
            section.<x>Failed',…)><Child/></SectionErrorBoundary>
            → DriveDetailSectionBoundary(section:status:onRetry:content:) — renders
              the injected child unit when .ready, a compact skeleton when .loading,
              and the EXACT web fallback title + Retry when .failed / no child
              (never a blank region). The 19 fallback titles live on
              DriveDetailSection.fallbackTitleKey/Default (Model).
  order:  the web JSX order + grouping + the four conditional gates are reproduced
            1:1 in DriveDetailPage.sections(_:) and pinned by
            DriveDetailSectionPlanTests.testFullPlanOrderWithTelemetryEnergyAndID:
            header · [banner] · heroGauges(stats) · timeline · statCards(stats) ·
            aiCoaching · moreDetails(stats) · energySummary(stats) ·
            costSavings(energy>0) · routeMap · journeyDetails · [chart group:
            overviewChart · {socChart|elevationChart} · {temperature|speedHistogram}
            · aiSpeedProfile · powerProfile] · tirePressure · whyEnded(id).
  charts grid: web `grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2` → adaptivePair(_:_:) — two-up
            on a wide (macOS/iPad regular) window, stacked on a compact iPhone
            width (@Environment horizontalSizeClass; macOS = wide). ADR-002 one
            adaptive source for macOS + iOS.
  nav:    web <Route path="/drives/:id"> + <Link>s → DriveDetailDestination value +
            .driveDetailNavigationDestination() on the NavigationStacks +
            DriveDetailDeepLink.destination(forPath:) (parses /drives/:id) +
            DriveDetailPageFactory (builds the shell from the route id — the page
            renders from navigation values / local state, no API per the manifest).
  i18n:   table "DriveDetailPage" via the P1/S10 facade DriveDetailPageStrings —
            the 23 web keys (verbatim, defaults reconciled with web/src/i18n/en.json)
            + native shell chrome (loading/empty/errorTitle/retry/sectionRetry).
  telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"DriveDetailPage") emitted exactly once on
            appear (asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnce).
  a11y:   per-section accessibilityIdentifier, combined header summary
            (DriveDetailPageAccessibility.summary), decorative glyphs hidden,
            Dynamic Type via tokens, Reduce-Motion via TSSkeleton, light/dark +
            increased-contrast via the generated dynamic-color tokens.
  units:  SI on the wire (distanceM / maxSpeedMps / energyWh) — the shell never
            converts; display conversion is the child units' boundary concern.

STATES (every one renders — verified by the ImageRenderer tests [6/6]):
  loading → DriveDetailPageSkeleton (header + stat-grid + 2 chart blocks).
  empty   → DriveDetailPageEmptyView (ContentUnavailableView, "Drive Details").
  error   → DriveDetailPageErrorView (danger glyph + message + Retry).
  content → the ordered section stack (two flavours: with telemetry = every
            numeric panel + cost savings; without telemetry = the info banner
            replaces the four numeric panels, matching the web envelope).
  section → DriveDetailSectionBoundary states ready / loading / failed(fallback).

